<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-01: Engine container image + ADR-004 A2 queue-consumer entrypoint + golden-fixture parity test</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations and cleanup</phase>
    <gate>blocked — external PR #3163 (accelerator engines on master) and task 007 (ADR-004 A2 on master, or in the same PR)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates new code (Python entrypoint, Dockerfile) for the first consumer outside the BFF; idempotency and dead-letter guarantees are fail-open/data-loss risks (NFR-01); 6+ steps.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New pattern authoring: the first ADR-004 A2 consumer outside the BFF (no in-repo reference implementation), with an atomic-marker idempotency design, lock renewal across long engine runs, and explicit dead-lettering that need judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P0-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>007, 002</deps>
    <tags>backend, azure, infrastructure, worker, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the engine container: a Dockerfile and a Python 3.11 entrypoint in `src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/` that runs the accelerator's `segment_clauses`, `ooxml_redline`, `summary_table` and `check_outputs` UNCHANGED from `src/accelerators/core/engines/` on master, as an ADR-004 A2 Service Bus consumer reading and writing stamp-private blob storage with the job's managed identity. Prove it with a golden-fixture parity test on synthetic NDAs.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Python 3.11, Docker, Azure Container Apps Jobs, and the Azure Python SDKs (azure-identity, azure-servicebus, azure-storage-blob) with managed identity. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/` contains a Dockerfile (repo-root build context; COPYs the engines from `src/accelerators/core/engines/` at build time, never vendored into this folder), an entrypoint package implementing the five A2 guarantees, and stdlib `unittest` tests: envelope validation, marker idempotency, deterministic paths, outcome reporting, and golden parity (container output byte-identical to a local run of the same engine version on the synthetic corpus).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01 (acceptance a–g), NFR-01, NFR-03, NFR-06, NFR-10; design §5 (owner decision A, conditions 2–3); ADR-004 A2 (drafted on this branch, task 007 merges it). The job is a pure engine: no BFF calls, no secrets, network only to Blob and Service Bus. Content travels by claim check (blob), never in the message. The BFF side (dispatch, completion handling) is task 014; infra is task 002; CI image build is task 003. Folder convention: `src/server/services/` already holds the only other container (`Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Sidecar/`), so it is used instead of the proposed `src/server/workers/intake-engine/` (no `src/server/workers/` exists).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/Dockerfile</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/main.py</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/envelope.py</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/azure_io.py</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/requirements.txt</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/tests/test_envelope_and_marker.py</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/tests/test_golden_parity.py</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Sidecar/Dockerfile (base-image pinning, non-root user, header rationale)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/JobContract.cs (the envelope fields and camelCase wire shape to validate against; MaxDeliveryCount at :65)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/accelerators/core/engines/*.py and src/accelerators/core/engines/tests/test_engines.py (on master after #3163; confirmed in the accelerator worktree, NOT yet on this branch)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/accelerators/practices/nda/evals/corpus/nda-0{1,2,3}-*.docx, src/accelerators/practices/nda/evals/expected/nda-01-golden-plan.json (synthetic corpus and golden plan; after #3163)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="007" status="pending">ADR-004 A2 merged to master before this code merges, or in the same PR (FR-04).</dependency>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">Queue names, staging container name and MI client id used by the entrypoint's configuration.</dependency>
      <dependency task="external-#3163" status="pending">Engines, schemas and synthetic corpus on master.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: the entrypoint. It MUST satisfy A2 §2 items 1–5: reject a non-envelope message to the DLQ with no outputs; take an atomic marker (conditional blob create with `If-None-Match: *`, keyed by `idempotencyKey`) before writing outputs; write outputs to deterministic paths derived from ids in the payload so a replay overwrites; carry `correlationId` into every log line and the completion message; report Completed / Failed / Poisoned.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: every message the entrypoint reads or sends. Payloads carry ids, blob paths and flags only — never document bytes, edit-plan text or clause text (A2 §3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: all logs, telemetry and completion messages emitted by the entrypoint. Identifiers, outcome codes and durations only; no document text, clause text, file names from the document, or edit-plan content.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: all Azure calls. Managed identity tokens only (Container Apps `IDENTITY_ENDPOINT`/`IDENTITY_HEADER`, user-assigned client id from config); no keys, connection strings or SAS; no BFF endpoint calls; no reference to `Sprk.Bff.Api`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the engines. They run on Python 3.11 with the standard library + `lxml` only, exactly as the accelerator ships them. The engines are COPYed from `src/accelerators/core/engines/` in the Docker build; no engine file is copied into, forked or edited in this project.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the entrypoint (wrapper) layer only. It uses the pinned Azure SDKs `azure-identity` (ManagedIdentityCredential with the UAMI client id), `azure-servicebus` (peek-lock receive, `AutoLockRenewer`, complete, abandon, explicit `dead_letter_message` with reason and description) and `azure-storage-blob` (get, put, conditional create with `if_none_match="*"`). Versions pinned with hashes in `requirements.txt` and installed with `pip install --require-hashes`; nothing else is added. Owner decision 2026-11-25 (design §5 Condition 1, spec FR-01): explicit dead-lettering with a reason, lock renewal past the 5-minute maximum Service Bus lock for runs up to the 10-minute timeout, and maintained token and retry handling are A2 requirements that hand-written REST would re-implement in security-sensitive code. The engines' stdlib + lxml rule is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: consistency with the BFF's `ServiceBusJobProcessor` and `JobSubmissionService` (owner direction 2026-11-25, "consistent with other components"), so DLQ admin, re-drive and telemetry treat the engine queue the same as the BFF queues.
      (a) **Dead-letter reason codes:** the BFF vocabulary only (`ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs:179,249,283`): `InvalidFormat` for a non-envelope message, `Poisoned`, `MaxRetriesExceeded` and `ProcessingError`. Descriptions carry codes and ids only.
      (b) **Retries:** the logical delivery count is the `PriorDeliveryCount` application property plus the broker `delivery_count` (`JobContract.cs` `PriorDeliveryCountProperty`). A retryable failure sends a scheduled copy carrying the updated `PriorDeliveryCount`, delayed per `JobContract.RetryDelay` (1, 2, 4, 8 minutes), then completes the original. At logical delivery `JobContract.MaxDeliveryCount` (5) it dead-letters `MaxRetriesExceeded`. Do not use bare abandon for retries.
      (c) **Outgoing messages** (retry copies and the completion message): `message_id` = the envelope's `idempotencyKey`, `correlation_id` = `correlationId`, `content_type` = `application/json`, `subject` = `jobType`, as `JobSubmissionService.cs:109-114` sets them.
      (d) **Telemetry:** the hash-pinned `azure-monitor-opentelemetry` distro exports to the stamp's App Insights (`APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING`, set by task 002), the same Azure Monitor OpenTelemetry pipeline as the BFF's `UseAzureMonitor()`. `correlationId`, `jobId` and `jobType` are attributes on every log record and span; outcomes are logged as `Completed` / `Failed` / `Poisoned` (`JobOutcome.cs`).
      (e) **Job types** are PascalCase nouns in the `JobTypeName` style: the request is `IntakeEngineRun`, and the completion is `IntakeEngineCompleted` (task 014).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the Dockerfile. It follows the sidecar's documented format (`src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Sidecar/Dockerfile`): a header stating purpose, runtime model, attack surface and what is deliberately absent; the base pinned by digest; a non-root user; and an image-size ceiling stated in the header and enforced by the CI size step (task 003).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: all tests and fixtures. Synthetic NDAs only (the accelerator's `evals/corpus/` synthetic files). Never read the accelerator `answer-key/` or any real NDA (NFR-10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">Scope: the job. Function-equivalent guardrails: stateless, bounded runtime (10-minute hard timeout from spec Assumptions), retries bounded by MaxDeliveryCount then a monitored DLQ.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
