    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Container image header and pinning" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Sidecar/Dockerfile">Pinned base by digest, non-root user, header comment stating purpose and scan posture.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Job Contract envelope" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/JobContract.cs">Field names and required fields the Python validator mirrors (JSON is the contract; no shared types, A2 §2).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm #3163 is merged and `src/accelerators/core/engines/` exists on master; confirm 007 is merged or will ride in the same PR. If not, stop (gate).</step>
    <step order="2">Write `entrypoint/envelope.py`: parse and validate the Job Contract envelope (required fields per JobContract.cs; `jobType` must equal the engine job type agreed with task 014, e.g. `IntakeEngineRun`); payload schema = ids and blob paths only.</step>
    <step order="3">Write `entrypoint/azure_io.py` over the pinned SDKs: `ManagedIdentityCredential(client_id=...)`; Service Bus peek-lock receive of ONE message with an `AutoLockRenewer` covering the full run (max renewal duration ≥ the 10-minute timeout), complete, abandon, and `dead_letter_message(reason=..., error_description=...)` with codes only (no content); Blob get, put, and conditional create (`if_none_match="*"`) for the marker. Write `requirements.txt` with pinned versions and hashes.</step>
    <step order="4">Write `entrypoint/main.py`: receive one message → validate → atomic marker → download inputs to a temp dir → run the four engines via their documented CLI → upload outputs to deterministic paths → send a Job Contract completion message (ids, outcome, check-report path) → complete the message. Invalid envelope → dead-letter path with no outputs.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the Dockerfile (python:3.11-slim pinned by digest, `lxml` pinned, non-root, repo-root context, COPY engines + entrypoint only).</step>
    <step order="6">Write tests: envelope accept/reject, marker taken once on duplicate, deterministic paths, refused edit appears in the check report and is not applied, golden parity (engines run locally vs. inside the built image on the 3 synthetic NDAs with the same plan; byte-compare outputs).</step>
    <step order="7">Build the image locally and run the tests; run a local Trivy scan and record the result.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations and the CLI contract used in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the pinned Azure SDKs (or `lxml`) introduce a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL CVE that no available pinned version resolves, STOP and escalate with the scan output; do not drop to hand-written REST and do not suppress the finding.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the engine CLI contract on master differs from what this task assumes, or an engine change would be needed, STOP and message the accelerator session "acclerator-r1"; never edit or fork the engines.</trigger>
    <trigger>If container output is not byte-identical to the local run, STOP and record the diff in notes; do not normalise outputs to make the test pass.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 7 (Container Apps / KEDA / server-side Python): none found; CAPABILITY-INDEX row 6 (queue background work) covers only in-BFF `IJobHandler`. Closest container precedent: `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Sidecar/Dockerfile`.</existing>
    <extension>No — the BFF cannot host Python + lxml, and ADR-052 forbids the job referencing `Sprk.Bff.Api`, so no existing consumer can be extended (ADR-004 A2 §1).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No server-side marked-up NDA exists: FR-09 has no engine to call, and the owner-approved option A (design §5) cannot run without a C# port the owner rejected.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="docker">Build and run the image locally</tool>
    <tool name="python">Python 3.11 `python -m unittest` (use `py -3.11` on Windows; never `python3`)</tool>
    <tool name="trivy">Local image scan</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/Dockerfile</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/main.py</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/envelope.py</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/entrypoint/azure_io.py</output>
    <output type="config">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/requirements.txt</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/tests/test_envelope_and_marker.py</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Intake.EngineJob/tests/test_golden_parity.py</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the 3 synthetic NDAs and the golden plan, when the engines run inside the image, then every output (redline, external, clean, check report) is byte-identical to a local run of the same engine version and `check_outputs` passes (FR-01a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a message that is not a valid envelope (missing field, wrong `jobType`, payload carrying content) is dead-lettered and no blob is written (FR-01b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same message delivered twice, then the marker is created once and one set of outputs exists at the same deterministic paths (FR-01c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An edit whose anchor is not unique or crosses an existing revision is listed in the check report and not applied (FR-01g).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every log line and the completion message carry `correlationId`; a grep of captured test logs finds no document or clause text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The image contains Python 3.11, `lxml`, the hash-pinned Azure SDK packages from `requirements.txt` (entrypoint layer only) and the unchanged engine files; no engine module imports an Azure SDK, and no file under `src/accelerators/` is modified by this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an engine run longer than the queue lock duration (simulated with a short lock in the test), the message lock is renewed and the message is completed once, not redelivered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an invalid envelope is dead-lettered with reason `InvalidFormat` (not by lock expiry), and the reason and description contain no document content.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a retryable engine failure on logical delivery 1–4, a scheduled copy is sent with `PriorDeliveryCount` incremented and the `JobContract.RetryDelay` delay, and the original is completed. On logical delivery 5 the message is dead-lettered `MaxRetriesExceeded`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The completion message carries `message_id` = idempotencyKey, `correlation_id`, `content_type` `application/json` and `subject` = `IntakeEngineCompleted`, and its body parses as a Job Contract the BFF's `ServiceBusJobProcessor` accepts (camelCase fields per `JobContract.cs`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The image has no secrets, and its code calls only the MI token endpoint, Blob and Service Bus hosts (FR-01f); a local Trivy scan reports no fixable HIGH/CRITICAL (FR-01d, enforced in CI by task 003).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test reads the accelerator `answer-key/` or a real NDA (NFR-10).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Seeding proof requested for the marker test only (a broken marker is a duplicate-output / data-loss outcome): remove the `If-None-Match` condition, confirm the duplicate test fails, restore. Latency measurement on dev (FR-01e) belongs to task 008. The completion-message destination is decided with task 002/014 (see 002 notes: the BFF's existing jobs queue, since `ServiceBusJobProcessor` is single-queue).</notes>

